#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197978 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of a Rod About the Origin"}] :question/id #uuid "cb13bd5e-ec8a-5e5c-a45f-d710ced8c3ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-12473" :question/problem "The thin rod below has the mass density function $\\lambda (x) = (x+4)\\,\\textrm{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/7f88ca365b75320795e9d38170a8586399d759696638a4bd78c73ca6c6f44b1a.png)" :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda(x)$ for $a \\leq x \\leq b$ is given by \n\n$$\nM_O = \\int_a^b x\\, \\lambda(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x) = x+4, \\qquad \na=0, \\qquad \nb=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot (x+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}+4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+2\\cdot {3}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $27\\,\\textrm{kg}\\cdot \\textrm{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197979 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass of a Rod"}] :question/id #uuid "4ebe8c87-95ba-58e2-b5d4-1bb19f231dc1" :question/math-academy-id "e-12474" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/461c4cb760541ea435620803689e193d13c9cb4706a59b031d37da6ffd49ab9f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x) = x^3.$ Given that the rod's mass is $4$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a \\leq x \\leq b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda(x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\int_a^b \\lambda (x) \\: \\textrm{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_O = \\int_a^b \\, x\\lambda (x) \\: \\textrm{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x) = x^3, \\qquad \na=0, \\qquad \nb=2.\n$$\n\nSo,  the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(32-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overline{x}= \\dfrac{M_O}{m} = \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{32}{5}\\right)}{4} = \\dfrac{8}{5}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that this result makes intuitive sense. Since $\\lambda$ is an increasing function of $x,$ we would expect the center of mass to be located closer to the right endpoint and further from the left endpoint."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197980 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Mass of a Thin Rod"}] :question/id #uuid "5c469b72-7ee3-5084-be63-2b7e62b42146" :question/math-academy-id "e-12475" :question/problem "The thin rod below has the mass density function $\\lambda(x) =2x\\, \\textrm{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/8c8386ff979b46cd994f1ace60f681a6590856e6960e7d74c71a29bb3f0f2d1a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a \\leq x \\leq b,$ if $\\lambda(x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm = \\int_a^b \\lambda(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x) = 2x, \\qquad \na=1, \\qquad \nb=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{2}]_{1}^{3} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $8\\,\\textrm{kg}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of a Rod About the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f64918a-aa67-57da-a49d-a064737ee08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351339} {:answer/id #uuid "d4cf2436-01bf-524c-ae30-d9a646b4192f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351340} {:answer/id #uuid "db508f40-59c5-5289-b494-b3a62dcc10bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351341} {:answer/id #uuid "bc1a85e7-6409-5c20-aac7-8e770bf6d76c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351342} {:answer/id #uuid "ac143dd4-4405-5688-9d97-ff459d4582f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac143dd4-4405-5688-9d97-ff459d4582f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351343} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f7a8dc4-cc36-515c-899d-27c490389e7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ae9b639-ddf7-5a21-a2c9-715cb70d087a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162948" :question/problem "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=4{x}^{2},$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=4{x}^{2},\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot 4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{4}-{1}^{4} \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass of a Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aed4dff9-c500-59ad-b94a-8e2b32b21454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194304} {:answer/id #uuid "c0dde479-38d3-5595-9980-463ae5d6d87e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194305} {:answer/id #uuid "f210d88f-b395-5391-be7d-70ba0d5628b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194306} {:answer/id #uuid "29e4ae9d-1bdb-566d-a4e4-918e4eda5351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194307} {:answer/id #uuid "423a1633-2ba6-54b9-9fd4-7778b05e9052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29e4ae9d-1bdb-566d-a4e4-918e4eda5351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194307} :answer-field/id #uuid "063a6123-d8f9-5157-acb7-3c575af4c824" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2b48c642-16a8-5d6a-818c-93071a473cf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-162957" :question/problem "Consider a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 2$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=3x.$ Given that the rod's mass is $6$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3x,\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot 3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =8-0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{8}{6}=\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351344 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass of a Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaba3ad6-c108-5ed6-9212-15d5c0cd34cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351346} {:answer/id #uuid "4273ca3d-0355-50bc-9870-61cf6d377c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351347} {:answer/id #uuid "85e5472e-4f59-57b0-8852-7a8d2e6e0843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351348} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3a311d-5a1e-5425-9566-352f6febc698" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351349} {:answer/id #uuid "e2efb028-c4d5-5671-9bc1-3c07e556802d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2efb028-c4d5-5671-9bc1-3c07e556802d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351350} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc8b43c7-5669-51d0-926d-c16a7838488d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0d991181-2738-52fe-8913-289426ec5b40" :question/math-academy-id "q-162981" :question/problem "Consider a thin rod along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 4$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=\\sqrt{x}.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass of the rod." :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\sqrt{x},\\,a=0,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the mass of the rod is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {4}^{3/2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\cdot \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot {4}^{5/2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{64}{5})}{(\\frac{16}{3})}=\\frac{12}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Mass of a Thin Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80fc6ef4-37f7-5889-8cd3-307d54f097fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351353} {:answer/id #uuid "c292c459-aa87-5c26-aa31-2687886ea3ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351354} {:answer/id #uuid "10d5a9a1-0f0f-5952-bdc3-14690dd35c74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351355} {:answer/id #uuid "a1df0822-126e-5b10-a1db-21188dc8bec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351356} {:answer/id #uuid "463abff5-66d0-55c3-9a67-478ade03c844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c292c459-aa87-5c26-aa31-2687886ea3ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351354} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1775140-24bb-5fe2-9572-f36ce5269808" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc411752-e7d5-5473-a92e-af7ce4235eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-163013" :question/problem "The mass density function $\\lambda ,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ of a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2$ is given by $\\lambda (x)=3{x}^{2}+1,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by  \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3{x}^{2}+1,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}+x]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =({2}^{3}+2)-({1}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $8\\,\\text{kg}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass of a Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04eba856-0799-5bf4-9634-5e476b6469d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{e-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351360} {:answer/id #uuid "295404d0-cf33-5d75-82fe-eceede4f9284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351361} {:answer/id #uuid "ddc60c7f-fa54-5aaa-b1ab-59703a193cb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351362} {:answer/id #uuid "23596538-9f89-5745-9b75-6db8e3995fde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351363} {:answer/id #uuid "73d2ccaf-a34c-5bb5-b9b8-f8fa4ca3594a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23596538-9f89-5745-9b75-6db8e3995fde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351363} :answer-field/id #uuid "aff35934-5480-5c7f-9ed7-d1aec7bc49e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351359}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db4151bb-178b-55fb-96c6-b5798c6d3993" :question/math-academy-id "q-163016" :question/problem "Consider a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le e$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Given that the rod's mass is $1$ unit, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,a=1,\\,b=e.\n$$\n\nSo, the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =e-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{e-1}{1}=e-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass of a Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcb55e2c-5a1d-5c94-aa07-6df8e1243983" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351367} {:answer/id #uuid "590747f0-3390-59a9-bcfb-336154057fa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351368} {:answer/id #uuid "f562bc8d-9de9-551c-bb52-8f61c3c5b019" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351369} {:answer/id #uuid "de7d8e04-be88-5c88-b506-a252c526fbde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351370} {:answer/id #uuid "d9fadb95-93b4-5e40-bb4d-b894be05ecbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9fadb95-93b4-5e40-bb4d-b894be05ecbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351371} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fe72d6a-b3a2-5534-8650-7399e9ca1230" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc0cd8c9-d9c9-59c8-af1b-b823ec38fb53" :question/math-academy-id "q-163019" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/887bc91e2565fa24630af4cb74b28723783e31f4769495f0a28a622d73d176de.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=x+{x}^{2}.$ Given that the mass of the rod is $\\frac{5}{6}$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=x+{x}^{2},\\,a=0,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nSo,  the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot (x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{7}{12})}{(\\frac{5}{6})}=\\frac{7}{10}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351372 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass of a Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f931466c-2aae-56ac-8d4e-2932f606b89f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351374} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e69c4b-f2fb-56e6-9009-be08e6e2172b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351375} {:answer/id #uuid "1524654e-ddbb-53b9-ac21-8632618dbb35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351376} {:answer/id #uuid "280e4b0c-fcb9-5957-ae7f-92daacca68f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351377} {:answer/id #uuid "6c474f81-31d9-5f59-b444-b5bb64d5eb0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "280e4b0c-fcb9-5957-ae7f-92daacca68f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351377} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eaa02c2-f3ef-5756-a6a3-3874cf4e1b7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5747675c-28bb-5974-9009-1516474ab751" :question/math-academy-id "q-163022" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/54e5dd5fdea01c02b968a6040068e190676841cb8d7b7fc05c561e02d522bbf1.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}.$ Given that the mass of the rod is $\\frac{15}{32}$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}},\\,a=1,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nSo,  the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{3}{4})}{(\\frac{15}{32})}=\\frac{8}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351379 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Mass of a Thin Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00a1d592-1232-50d2-af2f-55d1e668817c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351381} {:answer/id #uuid "528d87c7-a383-5408-83cb-5c005805f511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351382} {:answer/id #uuid "8523eb1e-51d4-571b-91a0-a2bc5230f09e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351383} {:answer/id #uuid "f0cfba89-3ce3-5659-838e-728c888039de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351384} {:answer/id #uuid "48a3c1b7-21e2-5baf-bae6-140abb3a628c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8523eb1e-51d4-571b-91a0-a2bc5230f09e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351383} :answer-field/id #uuid "4237cfbe-c857-54ef-8c26-c86a6fe55c3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c027f14f-4add-545b-a1e6-658b8f9d8813" :question/math-academy-id "q-163023" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/d0e2bd46bf7db6e20f321383e8e0440a2a86f263ce5eb256d20db71f5c632e27.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=6{x}^{2}-10\\,\\text{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6{x}^{2}-10,\\,a=2,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}6{x}^{2}-10\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{x}^{3}-10x]_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 27-10\\cdot 3)-(2\\cdot 8-10\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $28\\,\\text{kg}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Mass of a Thin Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1bd2b04-4740-54f7-87dc-3308ef66e689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351388} {:answer/id #uuid "f28bb641-56b2-53ea-82f3-37f5e46f2a7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351389} {:answer/id #uuid "b819fb76-f0bb-52a8-b292-01d9688c70d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351390} {:answer/id #uuid "801c2fb8-b57a-5d1c-9b4c-c0cbe3e22eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351391} {:answer/id #uuid "2074fe48-f43c-5b33-8df8-a17036cac77c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2074fe48-f43c-5b33-8df8-a17036cac77c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351392} :answer-field/id #uuid "349f921d-73c7-5ab0-ab4f-20aa5eca12cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ccca339-64f3-5137-9985-a212fbf787d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-163024" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/d64311921135cf8dea0ec70bb0a83909fb1dba52664f4d6080de596be1693d5e.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}},\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}8{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-4{x}^{-2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{4}{1}) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $3\\,\\text{kg}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Mass of a Thin Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "199e930f-42a2-514c-93be-b747ea5cc420" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351395} {:answer/id #uuid "92da2784-bc65-5fa0-b114-edeb65061c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351396} {:answer/id #uuid "bcfde3e2-1c11-5354-a9f6-c5cace3b08ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351397} {:answer/id #uuid "2545c8fa-8dc0-5b48-9d05-139a622037d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351398} {:answer/id #uuid "b465ec99-ee85-5e03-a67b-6a865f8facd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "199e930f-42a2-514c-93be-b747ea5cc420" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351395} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b59cb92-eaa9-5e25-8c0c-18553a2d5817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351394}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4aa00abd-44ce-5eec-8222-ab2ef2eb803d" :question/math-academy-id "q-163027" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/32500120ed36acde90f5b27c44a6cf45f2d4766bacb5eb097debc0cd7117f27f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=3{x}^{2}-x\\,\\text{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3{x}^{2}-x,\\,a=1,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}3{x}^{2}-x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(27-\\frac{9}{2})-(1-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $22\\,\\text{kg}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351400 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Mass of a Thin Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46a13283-a80d-5f5f-be82-25bfa0680244" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351402} {:answer/id #uuid "5e0662a7-dccd-5c84-83f6-c0b4f5367a1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351403} {:answer/id #uuid "227f31b3-e1b2-57d8-8e41-7ea14a125c6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351404} {:answer/id #uuid "f7e3a1e3-a2da-51af-bc03-3d0db677f0e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351405} {:answer/id #uuid "5051d321-4cea-5b3f-b9e2-0a6073c7e6bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46a13283-a80d-5f5f-be82-25bfa0680244" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351402} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3bff5ee-5c71-5a68-adf4-816454d0d3fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33dc2ea2-d00c-5e39-945c-160ac13a087f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163030" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/ca0ff396606039accf8c3acb4fd1b8e505dd16d2fe9b765fcd5c043d1538a573.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=2{x}^{3}\\,\\text{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=2{x}^{3},\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{4}}{2}-0 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $8\\,\\text{kg}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351407 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of a Rod About the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c93a7a6-90fb-5930-b090-ce19a9936965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351409} {:answer/id #uuid "93871334-7775-52a4-aed7-3c5f84b07edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351410} {:answer/id #uuid "61eb5ea7-4724-5d42-b74f-ac12f085d3bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351411} {:answer/id #uuid "0037044b-3072-527e-8ac2-1b376f743163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351412} {:answer/id #uuid "7df42914-ac94-5d0b-a1c3-856170711096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7df42914-ac94-5d0b-a1c3-856170711096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351413} :answer-field/id #uuid "735e2c7f-3a8c-564a-b6a9-508b924dd3ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f5ebe42-9a69-55b4-85c3-da9b0cecac83" :question/math-academy-id "q-163036" :question/problem "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=6x,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6x,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot 6x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({2}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of a Rod About the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12bf9c26-f0e3-5951-a5e8-e9f8033e8147" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351416} {:answer/id #uuid "89436c32-92c9-5406-ad2d-4a625a0d3835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351417} {:answer/id #uuid "e08ece88-bbe1-5197-859b-2bb1d4ed0ccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351418} {:answer/id #uuid "38178331-bb47-587b-8899-fce443d7aefa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351419} {:answer/id #uuid "e464e2d9-6878-55c4-bf74-25881ea61159" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12bf9c26-f0e3-5951-a5e8-e9f8033e8147" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351416} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa5b343b-f410-5840-a849-0c64eb6a7b73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2c0bfdd-0747-5e9c-ade1-1661720da9c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-163039" :question/problem "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=3x+1,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3x+1,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot (3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{2}+x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(8+\\frac{4}{2})-(1+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2} \\\\  & =8.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $8.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of a Rod About the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8d19e1b-691e-5b22-84f2-663e51aad86c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351423} {:answer/id #uuid "c9b21594-5ff0-5192-8418-6c00c35d555d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351424} {:answer/id #uuid "54a57188-be39-5dbd-ab67-7d55d1cd5cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351425} {:answer/id #uuid "dbcffca4-4f0e-5ffe-b015-f90cb18f3473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351426} {:answer/id #uuid "4c95a514-9354-571a-8661-02ccca1cccae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9b21594-5ff0-5192-8418-6c00c35d555d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351424} :answer-field/id #uuid "6647b0fe-5337-5e18-b21e-d07d66a446e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "51ab33b6-8bc7-58e3-84d1-57c89b0da879" :question/math-academy-id "q-163041" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/7f88ca365b75320795e9d38170a8586399d759696638a4bd78c73ca6c6f44b1a.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=4-x\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=4-x,\\,a=0,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot (4-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(2\\cdot {3}^{2}-\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3})-0 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of a Rod About the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bfb7aef-2535-5614-8990-0fd9216abd68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351430} {:answer/id #uuid "e5eb3add-382c-58dd-8d9e-68b4d7df20b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351431} {:answer/id #uuid "b87b4ab2-aa32-5249-9f3d-8a8062febefe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.75\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351432} {:answer/id #uuid "a96b22a2-8f81-5dd3-bc74-fff350f808f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351433} {:answer/id #uuid "16a47f28-3f8a-5961-be38-319e6e340b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5eb3add-382c-58dd-8d9e-68b4d7df20b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351431} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d9e1e9b-76ea-5975-90f1-5ba74e5c9122" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d42a6612-d0e8-534b-b07f-589486a9d686" :question/math-academy-id "q-163042" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/887bc91e2565fa24630af4cb74b28723783e31f4769495f0a28a622d73d176de.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=6x+{x}^{2}\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6x+{x}^{2},\\,a=0,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot (6x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{1}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =2.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $2.25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}]}
